Estimate the direct percent change in aggregate total factor productivity this quarter caused by this event, relative to an otherwise identical economy without it.
In the Krusell-Smith model, output is Y = Z * K^alpha with labour fixed at 1. Z is total factor productivity: output obtainable from unchanged quantities of capital and effective labour. Hold those quantities fixed. Exclude demand changes, changes in household willingness to consume, capital accumulation, and changes explained solely by hours worked or employment. Include only an event's effect on production efficiency at fixed inputs; use 0 if no such channel is supported by the narrative. Do not infer TFP directly from a change in GDP.
